course: dictionary
lesson: 332
title: Jobs behind the stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An animator is a person who makes cartoons, animated films and computer games. Animators create pictures that look like they move. Each small change in a picture helps a character move, so the animator makes many pictures.
explain: Read this sentence: «All three are slow: one second of cartoon can need a dozen or more pictures, so a few seconds can take an animator a whole day.» The clue is that a few seconds take a whole day. Animators must work very slowly and carefully, one picture at a time.
explain: Context also tells you what animators do. «Many artists and animators still draw by hand even when they also use computers.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? A person who draws moving pictures fits, so animator means that kind of person.
fact: An animator makes moving pictures for cartoons, films and computer games.
fact: «One second of cartoon can need a dozen or more pictures.» A dozen means twelve.
fact: Animators can draw by hand, model in clay or use computers.
fact: «Animators squash and stretch bodies because it looks lively and funny.»
fact: You can learn animation with flip books, stop-motion and coding apps.
exercise: «One second of cartoon can need a dozen or more pictures.» How many pictures is a dozen? | Ten | Two | *Twelve | Twenty
exercise: What is an animator? | A person who sells tickets at the cinema | A machine that plays music | *A person who makes animated films, cartoons or computer games | A teacher who only marks spelling tests
exercise: «Many artists and animators still draw by hand even when they also use computers.» What does this sentence tell us? | Animators never draw and only type | Animators always work alone in the dark | *Animators can still draw by hand, even when they use computers | Animators only work in banks
test: Which person in this list makes cartoons move? | Musician | Busker | Actor | *Animator
test: «A few seconds can take an animator a whole day.» What does this tell you about the work? | It takes one minute | *It is slow and takes a lot of patience | It is only done at weekends | It is fast and easy
exam: «Coders work far beyond games and tech firms.» Where do coders work, according to the sentence? | Only in games | Only in the sea | Only on the moon | *In banks, hospitals, farms and governments
